  "title": "So-called Temple of Cybele",
  "provenance": "Pleiades",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/temple-2"
  ],
  "details": "<p>Probably built around the second century CE, it showed initially a pronaos and a large cella. It was substantially changed after the earthquake in 262 CE, when the cult space was waterproofed to become a cistern, probably connected to the adjacent Shrine of the Meander Mosaic. It seems that it was completly destroyed by the earthquake of 365 CE.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A recently discovered temple on the acropolis of Cyrene.",
